# NorthNarrow COMBAT-state ip6tables ruleset (BUG-031 / block 2; BUG-041 additive).
#
# Loaded by NetworkIsolator::engage() via `ip6tables-restore --noflush`,
# ALONGSIDE the v4 ruleset. ADDITIVE (BUG-041): the `:NORTHNARROW_COMBAT`
# declaration atomically rebuilds OUR chain; the `-I … 1` jumps insert it
# on TOP of the operator's v6 rules; `--noflush` leaves operator chains
# untouched. Our chain is TERMINAL during COMBAT — it decides every v6
# packet, so operator rules sit beneath it, inert but PRESERVED, and are
# uncovered intact at teardown.
#
# Preserve-NDP (BUG-031): drops v6 DATA but keeps the stack alive. Unlike
# v4 (ARP is L2, outside the filter table), v6 NDP/MLD ride ICMPv6 IN this
# table, so a bare DROP would brick neighbour resolution (couldn't even
# reach the carve-out gateway). We ACCEPT the ICMPv6 control plane before
# the catch-all DROP.
#
# ACCEPT, not RETURN (BUG-041): under additive a RETURN would defer to the
# operator's rules, making the preserve-NDP + loopback guarantees depend
# on their config. ACCEPT (terminal) keeps the guarantees ours.
#
# Owned limit (BUG-031): this leaves an ICMPv6 NDP/MLD control channel
# open on the local segment during isolation (a same-segment attacker
# could in principle tunnel over it; a remote/routed one cannot).
#
# Beta Step 4b carve-out marker (same as v4): engage() replaces it with
# ip6tables `-j ACCEPT` rules for each IPv6 CIDR in combat-allow.cidrs.

*filter
:NORTHNARROW_COMBAT - [0:0]
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -i lo -j ACCEPT
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -o lo -j ACCEPT
# --- preserve the v6 stack: ICMPv6 control plane (drop DATA, not the stack) ---
# ICMPv6 errors + PMTUD: 1 dest-unreachable, 2 packet-too-big, 3 time-exceeded, 4 parameter-problem
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 1 -j ACCEPT
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 2 -j ACCEPT
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 3 -j ACCEPT
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 4 -j ACCEPT
# MLD: 130 query, 131 report (v1), 132 done, 143 report (v2) — multicast membership NDP depends on
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 130 -j ACCEPT
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 131 -j ACCEPT
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 132 -j ACCEPT
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 143 -j ACCEPT
# NDP: 133 router-solicit, 134 router-advert, 135 neighbour-solicit, 136 neighbour-advert, 137 redirect
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 133 -j ACCEPT
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 134 -j ACCEPT
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 135 -j ACCEPT
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 136 -j ACCEPT
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 137 -j ACCEPT
# >>> NORTHNARROW_MGMT_CARVEOUT <<<
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -j DROP
-I INPUT 1 -j NORTHNARROW_COMBAT
-I OUTPUT 1 -j NORTHNARROW_COMBAT
-I FORWARD 1 -j NORTHNARROW_COMBAT
COMMIT
